[38;5;252m[1m## What the C actually does[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The project has [1mno [38;5;10m[features][0m[22m — one configuration, which [38;5;10mverify.sh[0m re-derives from [38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m so a future feature would automatically be covered.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The load-bearing quirk: [38;5;10minclude/match.h[0m has [38;5;10mtypedef double float_t[0m, but [38;5;10msrc/spectral_contrast.c[0m includes only [38;5;10m<math.h>[0m and never [38;5;10mmatch.h[0m, so [3mits[23m [38;5;10mfloat_t[0m is C99's, i.e. [38;5;10mfloat[0m on x86-64. I confirmed this in the object code ([38;5;10mmovss[0m, 4-byte stride, [38;5;10mmulss[0m, [38;5;10mcvtss2sd[0m, [38;5;10mcvtsd2ss[0m). So [38;5;10mmatch[0m hands [38;5;10mdouble[0m scratch arrays to a callee that reads and writes them as [38;5;10mfloat[0ms, chewing through only the leading [38;5;10mbins * 4[0m bytes. The Rust already reproduced this.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;252m[1m## Fixes made[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m[38;5;10mCargo.toml[0m[22m — [38;5;10m[lib] name[0m was [38;5;10munderhanded-c-nuke_lib[0m; cargo rejects hyphens in library target names, so nothing built at all. Renamed to [38;5;10munderhanded_c_nuke_lib[0m (the [38;5;10m.so[0m filename is unchanged either way, since cargo maps hyphens to underscores). Added [38;5;10mlibloading[0m to [38;5;10m[dev-dependencies][0m.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1mNaN payload divergence ([38;5;10msrc/sse.rs[0m, new).[22m [38;5;10mspectral_contrast[0m returns a [38;5;10mdouble[0m straight to the caller, so its NaN [3mpayload bits[23m are observable — and NaNs arise routinely, because reinterpreting a [38;5;10mdouble[0m mantissa as a [38;5;10mfloat[0m hits exponent [38;5;10m0xFF[0m about 1 time in 256. IEEE 754 leaves the payload unspecified when several operands are NaN, but x86 does not: for [38;5;10mOP DEST, SRC[0m, a NaN [38;5;10mDEST[0m wins over a NaN [38;5;10mSRC[0m. GCC compiles [38;5;10msum += a[i] * b[i][0m as [38;5;10mmulss[0m with [38;5;10mb[i][0m as destination and [38;5;10maddsd[0m with the [3mwidened product[23m as destination, so the element beats the accumulator. Natural Rust operand order gives the opposite in both cases, and the returned NaN differed. Added explicit [38;5;10maddsd[0m/[38;5;10mmulsd[0m/[38;5;10mdivsd[0m/[38;5;10msubsd[0m/[38;5;10mmulss[0m helpers that pin the selection down rather than hoping operand order survives codegen, and used them in [38;5;10mdot_product[0m, [38;5;10mnormalize[0m, [38;5;10mtotal[0m, [38;5;10msmoothen[0m, [38;5;10mdifferentiate[0m, and the [38;5;10mthreshold * total(reference)[0m product.[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[1m[38;5;10msrc/spectral_contrast.rs[0m[22m — switched from [38;5;10m&mut [f32][0m slices to raw pointers. [38;5;10mspectral_contrast(p, p, n)[0m is legal C, and [38;5;10mnormalize(a); normalize(b)[0m on aliasing pointers created two overlapping [38;5;10m&mut[0m slices, which is Rust UB that [38;5;10mnoalias[0m can miscompile. There are now explicit tests for fully aliased and partially overlapping arguments.[0m[0m
