[38;5;252m[1m## One deliberate, documented difference[0m[0m
[0m[0m
[38;5;10mbins == 0[0m: the C declares [38;5;10mfloat_t t[0][0m and [38;5;10mdifferentiate[0m then executes [38;5;10mv[-1] = 0[0m, storing 8 bytes below [38;5;10mrsp[0m and destroying the return address. The C [38;5;10m.so[0m reliably segfaults — I verified this with a standalone [38;5;10mdlopen[0m driver. There is no defined behaviour to match, so that input is excluded from the C comparison; the test file records why, and asserts the Rust side returns [38;5;10m0.0 >= threshold[0m instead of crashing.[0m[0m
